"The announcement post for Claude 4 support in github copilot claims that the models feature thinking support: https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/159974\n>  Both models feature \"hybrid thinking\" capabilities, allowing them to engage in extended reasoning with tool use and produce logical summaries of their thought processes—making your coding experience even more intuitive and productive!\n\nHowever, it seems this is not the case for me as can be seen here:\n<img width=\"465\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c0a50763-dbd0-4ee4-9206-7bae2f23e76b\" />\n\nUnlike Claude 3.7 there is no option in the dropdown to select a \"thinking version\" of either Claude 4 model:\n<img width=\"255\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c00e12cc-6e06-4630-a99d-aadabe92cc67\" />\n\n- Copilot Chat Extension Version: latest\n- VS Code Version: latest\n- OS Version: MacOS (latest)\n- Feature (e.g. agent/edit/ask mode): All\n- Selected model (e.g. GPT 4.1, Claude 3.7 Sonnet): Either Claude 4 model\n- Logs: I'm not sure if any logs are relevant to this issue - please let me know if I need to provide any!\n\nSteps to Reproduce:\n1. Open chat menu and talk to a Claude 4 model.\n","closed_by":{"login":"bhavyaus","id":25044782,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MDQ0Nzgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25044782?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus","html_url":"https://github.com/bhavyaus","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bhavyaus/repos","events_url":"https: